The wild strawberry is used as an indicator plant for diseases that affect the garden strawberry. It is also used as a genetic [[Model organism|model plant]] for garden strawberry and the family Rosaceae in general, due to its:
*very small genome size
*short reproductive cycle (14–15 weeks in climate-controlled greenhouses)
*ease of propagation.

